OK, I took a quick look.  It looks like it works for integrals
on (-1, 1), so I see how it'd work for bounded integrals by scaling
and translating coordinates linearly.

But how would it work with integrals on (-inf, inf) or (0, inf)?
Would those have to be double exponential to start with?  Or
could we take a normal(0, 1), transform it to (-1, 1), then
work from there with a Jacobian?

Also, it looks like Bailey himself wrote a BSD version in C++:

  http://crd-legacy.lbl.gov/~dhbailey/mpdist/

though it's not clear which of those packages it'd be in.

