>
> though it's not clear which of those packages it'd be in.

Cook's version is fine, although Bailey may have some other good stuff in ARPREC. The problem with public domain is that nothing prevents someone else (like us) from slapping their own license on it. We'd have to rewrite a good bit of it anyway to make it work with Stan.

Ben

