From u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com  Tue Dec  1 22:39:06 2015
From: u8aa9b8cc06fdc99c at groups.google.com (Bob Carpenter)
Date: Tue, 01 Dec 2015 22:39:06 +0000
Subject: no namespace-level using statements
Message-ID: <BxBFV6donuU.Su5pIqhiBAAJ@stan-dev.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-dev/c/BxBFV6donuU/m/Su5pIqhiBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Please don't include namespace-level includes.

The problem is that then you can't control locally what
gets included, which can lead to name-resolution conflicts,
and it also introduces order dependencies on the files.

See:  http://stackoverflow.com/questions/6175705/scope-of-using-declaration-within-a-namespace

or go straight to Herb Sutter's advice:

  http://www.gotw.ca/gotw/053.htm

That site's awesome, by the way, if you want to study C++ :-)

- Bob

