Point taken; it's a bit tangential. This was the line of thinking: in
the stanc setting, dealing with error messages (parser errors) is
someone we do well with the current API. If we had a standard way of
reporting errors we could use it in other cases, e.g., when the
interface passed invalid algorithm parameters.

