cool use of the writer refactor (and it's come up in a few
conversations but Michael suggested waiting till the writer
refactor was done).

So far the list of suggested protobuf-related test projects looks like:
1) stanc server
2) shim for interfaces (say over just stanc to start)
3) standardizing error messages
4) streaming output using the current writer refactor-ed code.
5) adding callbacks parallel to the writer refactor so that protobuf messages could be produced

Part of my goal for starting this discussion on the mailing list was
to see if we can agree on which items deserve priority.

(I'm happy to do a simple version of 1) just as a demo regardless since the stanc
interface is so straightforward...)

