Thanks --- that clears things up a lot in terms
of the space you're thinking about.  I think all of
this is a good idea.

For (5), we'd just put write callbacks that wrote to
protocol buffers.

I think doing simple things first to get a handle for
how it works is a good idea.  The design's going to
be tangled up in the refactor design, so we should
keep this in mind.  I don't see any special problems
that writing to protocol buffers present --- in fact,
they solve many of the problems that other kinds of
writing (like to CSV files) have.  I particularly like
that they can be heterogeneously typed containers.

- Bob

