Cool --- that's the BSD 3-clause license, just like we
use for Stan and the Stan math lib.

This is very tightly interconnected with the refactor
of the core Stan functionality.  That's going to be
a C++ API.

Any protocol buffer interface would be layered on top of
the C++ API.  I don't understand enough about protocol
buffers or the interface languages to understand if it
would be easier to connect to protocol buffers that
connected to the underlying C++ than it would be to connect
to the underlying C++.

- Bob

