Hi Bob!

This sounds like a huge thing - is it worth investing this effort? Also, the deprecation period is hopefully very long, i.e. Stan programs will look very different wrt to BUGS programs with this.

My comments:

1. Why introduce another logic with "<norm=true/false>"? Do you plan to introduce further options here, then it makes sense. If only for discriminating between normed/unnormed I would prefer a _norm naming convention thing.

2. What is the rationale to introduce two new operators "<<" and ","? Maybe I haven´t understood fully, but writing

lp << density1 << density2;

makes more sense to me.

In any case, I suggest to try out this new scheme on people who are more statisticians than programmers, i.e. I think someone having a programming background will absorb this easily, but I am not so sure about those people without a programming background.

Best,
Sebastian

