It will return the log density.  Everything is on the log scale.

If you want the density, it's just exp(cauchy(y | mu, sigma)).

We don't currently have a function for the linear density, just
cauchy_log().  So the proposal is to replace "cauchy_log" with
"cauchy".  That's the most confusing part of this, but also
the thing that cleans up the notation the most.

- Bob

