I'm confused what this "keep" adds.  This is probably because I lost some other piece of context.  If user-defined densities have a <propto=true> or <propto=false>, then they need special treatment of some sort, otherwise they're just something you would otherwise pass to increment_log_prob()... no?  I guess they could increment ld as a side effect rather than returning the increment... but does it limit anything to disallow that? That's just a specialized version of increment_log_prob()...

> * Stan math lib suffixes (now "_log"; proposed keep)
>
> - Bob

